name unicode-special-casing
# SpecialCasing.txt. The header names the fields:
#   "# <code>; <lower>; <title>; <upper>; (<condition_list>;)? # <comment>"
#   "# The <condition_list> is optional. Where present, it consists of one or more language IDs"
#   "# or casing contexts, separated by spaces."
# Only the rows that carry a condition_list attest here: the rows without one are the full case mappings the
# XML gives as lc, tc and uc. A row says each of its mappings, as the text it is, and each condition of its list.
# A mapping the row leaves empty attests nothing.
match SpecialCasing.txt

tier row by \n
comment hash
remark hash
padded
names code lower title upper condition_list
tier field by ;
part condition_list by space

thing row code
range code
codepoints lower title upper
content condition_list
when condition_list matches [A-Za-z]
# The header: "This file is a supplement to the UnicodeData.txt file. The data in this file, combined with the simple case
# mappings in UnicodeData.txt, defines the full case mappings Lowercase_Mapping (lc), Titlecase_Mapping (tc), and
# Uppercase_Mapping (uc)." and "<code>, <lower>, <title>, and <upper> provide the respective full case mappings of <code>"
relation "Lowercase_Mapping" lower
relation "Titlecase_Mapping" title
relation "Uppercase_Mapping" upper
# The header: "The <condition_list> is optional. Where present, it consists of one or more language IDs or casing contexts,
# separated by spaces." "The condition list is not represented in the UCD as a formal property.": each condition a value
# of the file's own list (Final_Sigma, After_Soft_Dotted, More_Above, Before_Dot, After_I, Not_..., and BCP 47 language IDs)
value - condition_list
attest row lower title upper condition_list
# "A condition list overrides the normal behavior if all of the listed conditions are true": a row's mappings hold under
# its conditions, so they are one record, said together (the wiki's Unicode page: "with every condition of the list,
# together")
together row
